  "text": "The salmon is a mythic figure. In Celtic myth it is almost always a symbol of wisdom. Its long journey shapes that role. The fish hatches in an inland pool. It travels to the sea and lives there for years. Then it swims back to the very pool or stream where it was born. It spawns and dies there. That unerring return looks like hidden knowledge. The famous salmon of wisdom carries this idea. Fionn, still a boy, was set to tend it as it cooked. The poet Finnéces had caught it to gain all knowledge. The fish's hot oil burned Fionn's thumb, and he put it in his mouth. There the salmon's wisdom passed to him. From that day Fionn understood all he wished to know.",
